findings.fix:
Replace the `tcs.SetResult(); await Task.Delay(1);` pair with a deterministic wait for the guard to clear before the third click, e.g.:

    tcs.SetResult();
    cut.WaitForState(() => !cut.Find("button").HasAttribute("disabled"));
    cut.Find("button").Click();
    Assert.Equal(2, runCount);

(`IsDisabled` includes `_busy`, and completing the awaited EventCallback triggers a re-render, so the rendered `disabled` attribute is a reliable signal.) Do not use a fixed `Task.Delay`.
